.TH CORE-REPORT 1 "October 2026" "SASD Freeware" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
core-report \- inventory possible core dump files in a directory tree
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B core-report
.RI [ OPTIONS ] " DIRECTORY"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B core-report
lists regular files named
.B core
or beginning with
.BR core. .
Candidates are reported by name, not by inspecting their contents.
The original files are neither deleted nor changed.
Symbolic links are not followed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "--min-size " BYTES
Only list candidates of at least this many logical bytes.
.TP
.B --one-file-system
Skip entries on filesystems other than that of the scan root.
.TP
.B --null
Emit BYTES and PATH as successive NUL-terminated fields without summary.
.TP
.BR --help ", " -h
Display usage.
.TP
.B --version
Display version.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B core-report /var/tmp
Report matching regular files under /var/tmp.
.TP
.B core-report --min-size 1048576 /srv
List matching files of at least one mebibyte.
.SH OUTPUT
In text mode the first line contains BYTES and PATH, followed by candidates
and summary counts. Control characters are escaped in displayed paths.
In NUL mode all fields are delimited with NUL bytes.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 scan completed; 1 filesystem failure; 2 invalid arguments.
.SH NOTES
Reported files may not be actual core dumps. The scan may be inconsistent
if other processes change the directory tree during traversal. File sizes
are logical bytes, not allocated disk blocks.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR find (1),
.BR stat (1)
